From steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-snd: start the capture unit outside the capture lock

The capture start worker called AudioOutputUnitStart while holding the per-stream
`capture` mutex (patch 0017 published the unit under that lock and started it
inside the critical section). That call can block while the microphone is opened,
and on a fresh process it also arms the macOS microphone permission prompt, which
is not answered until the user clicks it. The pump thread takes `capture` every
iteration of the device loop, and it does so while the loop holds `hosts`; the
control-queue thread needs `hosts` to answer PREPARE/START/STOP. So a blocking
AudioOutputUnitStart wedged the pump, the pump held `hosts`, and *every* virtio-snd
control message timed out (PCM_PREPARE 0x103, PCM_RELEASE 0x102, PCM_START 0x104,
PCM_STOP 0x105) the moment the guest started recording. In VRChat this showed up as
a frozen game (main thread spinning) exactly when audio capture started, e.g. after a
graphics/resolution change reinitialised the audio device.

Start the unit before taking `capture` (the input callback reads the unit pointer
lock-free from `shared.unit`, which is set first). Publish under the lock afterwards
and, if a stop raced in while the unit was starting, stop it and publish nothing, so
a stop still takes down a unit that was running. No AudioUnit call now runs under
`capture`.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/devices/src/virtio/snd/audio_backends/coreaudio.rs | 40 +++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/devices/src/virtio/snd/audio_backends/coreaudio.rs b/src/devices/src/virtio/snd/audio_backends/coreaudio.rs
--- a/src/devices/src/virtio/snd/audio_backends/coreaudio.rs
+++ b/src/devices/src/virtio/snd/audio_backends/coreaudio.rs
@@ -1295,13 +1295,9 @@
         )?;
         let mut unit = unit;
         unit.initialize()?;
-        // Publish under the capture lock: a stop on the control thread either takes the
-        // published unit or, finding none while `starting` is set, leaves `stop_pending` for
-        // us to see here. The input callback needs the unit pointer, so it is set before the
-        // unit starts, not after.
-        let mut slot = shared.capture.lock().unwrap();
+        // A stop that arrived before this worker ran (found no published unit and left
+        // `stop_pending`) wants no unit started at all.
         if shared.stop_pending.swap(false, Ordering::AcqRel) {
-            drop(slot);
             return Ok(());
         }
         shared.capture_device.store(device, Ordering::Release);
@@ -1313,10 +1309,28 @@
                 staging: Vec::new(),
             },
         };
+        // The input callback needs the unit pointer before the unit starts producing; it reads
+        // it lock-free from `shared.unit`.
         shared.unit.store(state.unit.au, Ordering::Release);
+        // Start the unit WITHOUT holding `capture`: AudioOutputUnitStart can block while the
+        // microphone is opened (a permission prompt, a slow input device), and the pump thread
+        // takes `capture` every iteration while it holds `hosts`, which the control thread needs
+        // to answer PREPARE/START/STOP. Holding `capture` here would wedge every virtio-snd
+        // control message once the guest starts recording.
         if let Err(err) = state.unit.start() {
             shared.unit.store(ptr::null_mut(), Ordering::Release);
             return Err(err);
+        }
+        // Publish under the capture lock: a stop on the control thread either takes a
+        // previously published unit or, finding none while `starting` is set, leaves
+        // `stop_pending` for us to see here (that stop cannot stop a unit in `shared.unit`
+        // itself, so we do it). The unit is already running, so if a stop raced in, stop it.
+        let mut slot = shared.capture.lock().unwrap();
+        if shared.stop_pending.swap(false, Ordering::AcqRel) {
+            drop(slot);
+            state.unit.stop();
+            shared.unit.store(ptr::null_mut(), Ordering::Release);
+            return Ok(());
         }
         *slot = Some(state);
         Ok(())
